From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evan Liu <evliu@google.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:51:33 -0700
Subject: Skip loading system libspeechd.so.2 under MemorySanitizer

Speech Dispatcher is not built in //third_party/instrumented_libs, so
dlopen()ing the default system libspeechd.so.2 in MSan builds loads the
uninstrumented host library, which triggers false-positive MSan errors
when it calls into instrumented GLib.

Skip loading the default Speech Dispatcher library under MSan while
still allowing tests to override the path with an instrumented fake
library.

Fixed: 576859257
Change-Id: I89fd26f90b2e3c1066c281fa6aca690ff143e054
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8646789
Reviewed-by: Matthew Denton <mpdenton@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Evan Liu <evliu@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1726794}
Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
This branch's tts_linux.cc has no library-path override
(SpeechDispatcherLibraryPath()/SetSpeechDispatcherLibraryPathForTesting()
and the TtsPlatformImplBackgroundWorker library_path_ member come from a
later upstream change), so under MemorySanitizer InitializeSpeechd()
simply returns false and otherwise loads kDefaultSpeechDispatcherLibrary
as before. tts_linux_browsertest.cc does not exist on this branch and is
not carried.

diff --git a/content/browser/speech/tts_linux.cc b/content/browser/speech/tts_linux.cc
index dcfb2d419ccbaca3387672247643952c1a1708ef..491b9fcabef0ab70adafdaac8306bcb3c37dfdd2 100644
--- a/content/browser/speech/tts_linux.cc
+++ b/content/browser/speech/tts_linux.cc
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ using PlatformVoices = std::map<std::string, SPDChromeVoice>;
 
 constexpr int kInvalidUtteranceId = -1;
 constexpr int kInvalidMessageUid = -1;
+constexpr char kDefaultSpeechDispatcherLibrary[] = "libspeechd.so.2";
 
 }  // namespace
 
@@ -250,7 +251,15 @@ void TtsPlatformImplBackgroundWorker::Shutdown() {
 }
 
 bool TtsPlatformImplBackgroundWorker::InitializeSpeechd() {
-  return libspeechd_loader_.Load("libspeechd.so.2");
+#if defined(MEMORY_SANITIZER)
+  // Speech Dispatcher is not built in //third_party/instrumented_libs, so
+  // loading the default system library under MSan dlopens the uninstrumented
+  // host libspeechd.so.2, which triggers false-positive MSan errors when it
+  // calls into instrumented GLib.
+  return false;
+#else
+  return libspeechd_loader_.Load(kDefaultSpeechDispatcherLibrary);
+#endif
 }
 
 void TtsPlatformImplBackgroundWorker::InitializeVoices(PlatformVoices* voices) {
